🚽 Test case: #196 -- the struct-tag check applies to a `lit`-aliased
🚽 pointer declaration too, not just the direct `gang T *name = expr;`
🚽 spelling (PR #248 review, round 3, finding 1). `lit gang Point
🚽 *PointPtr; PointPtr pp = &r;` reaches semantic_visit_declaration()'s
🚽 GENERAL branch (data.op.right there IS the real initializer, unlike
🚽 the NODE_STRUCT_DEF-marker branch the round-2 fix covered) -- that
🚽 branch had the category check (VAR_STRUCT vs VAR_STRUCT) but no tag
🚽 check until now.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Rect {
    rizz w;
    rizz h;
};

lit gang Point *PointPtr;

skibidi main {
    gang Rect r;
    r.w = 11;
    r.h = 22;
    PointPtr pp = &r;
    yapping("%d %d", pp.x, pp.y);
}
